 

$************************RELEASE VERSION*********************************** 
$
$ mc_mg_v2.02.tdb
$
$************************RELEASE VERSION***********************************
$
$ MatCalc thermodynamic database for magnesium alloys.
$
$ Created 1.11.2023
$ (Release of previous version v2.01: 14.9.2023 by MatCalc Engineering GmbH.)
$
$ Update from version 2.01: 
$ Ba implementation
$ Alternative IM1 with improved dissolution T.
$ Y-Implementation (binaries Y-Al, Y-Mg, Y-Zn, Y-Zr, ternary Mg-Y-Zn)
$ Metastable binary Mg-Y, Y-Zn and ternary Mg-Y-Zn; clusters and beta prime.
$ Zr-Implementation (binaries Zr-Mg, Zr-Zn, Mg-Zn-Zr)
$ tentativ Y-Zn-Zr. NOTE: Mg-Y-Zr - NO ternary intermetallics.
$ This database contains edited and newly assessed thermodynamic data 
$ for Mg-base alloys.
$ Thermodynamic parameters have been assessed at TU Wien 
$ by Povoden-Karadeniz Erwin. 
$
$ #########################################################################
$
$ use with MatCalc version 6.00 or higher.
$
$ #########################################################################
$ 
$ Copyright and editor: Erwin Povoden-Karadeniz 
$ (erwin.povoden-karadeniz@tuwien.ac.at)
$
$ This database mc_mg_v2.01.tdb is made available under the 
$ Open Database License: http://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/. 
$ Any rights in individual contents of the database are licensed under the 
$ Database Contents License: http://opendatacommons.org/licenses/dbcl/1.0/. 
$
$ ##########################################################################

$ The following assessments are incorporated in this database:
$
$ ... see list of publications in the reference section 
$ at the end of this file ...


$ The following elements are included in this database:
$
$ Mg, Al, Ba, Ca, Mn, Si, Sr, Y, Zn, Zr

$ Ambit

$ This database version has been designed and tested to be used 
$ for thermokinetic simulations in AZ Mg-alloys 
$ from melting to room temperature. 
$ For kinetic simulations at low temperature, the low temperature limits 
$ of Gibbs energies were reduced from 298.15 K, as given by Ref 0, to 273.00 K.
$ High-T limit put to 6000K.
$ For kinetic simulations at very high temperatures, the high temperature limits 
$ of Gibbs energies were in some cases extended to higher temperatures 
$ than given by Ref 0.  
$ Binary Mg-X, Al-Ba, Ba,Ca, for DieMAg633 simulations. 
$ Ternary Al-Ca-Mn, Al-Ca-Si, Al-Ca-Sr, Al-Ca-Zn, Al-Mg-Sr, Al-Mn-Sr, 
$ Al-Si-X (except Al-Si-Mg), Al-Sr-X, Mg-Mn-Zn, Mg-Mn-Si, Mg-Si-Sr, Mn-Si-X, 
$ Mn-Sr-Zn, Si-Sr-Zn, and higher orders are ideal extension from the binaries.
$ Thermodynamic equilibrium calculations have been tested for wrought alloys 
$ with x(Mg) > 0.95.

$ The following phases are included in this database:
$
$ The following phases are included in this database:
$ They are listed in the order of their appearance in 
$ part D) Thermodynamic model parameters for phases. 
$ For their documentation see part D). 
$ Documentation and priority rankings suggested by the editor are visible 
$ in the MatCalc databases window after reading the database 
$ and marking the phase of interest.
$ 
$ LIQUID
$
$ Alloy phases
$ HCP_A3  HCP_ZN  BCC_A2  FCC_A1  ALPHA_MN  BETA_MN

$ intermetallic equilibrium phases listed in the same order 
$ as in section IV by relevance in Mg-alloys.

$ AL5BA4  AL13BA7  ALMG_BETA  ALMG_EPS  G_AL12MG17  ALMGMN_T  AL4MN  AL6MN  AL8MN5_D810  
$ AL11MN4  AL12MN  AL3X8  AL4X  AL14CA13  AL2SR  AL7SR8  C2M5Z13  C2M6Z3
$ CAZN  CAZN2  CAZN3  CAZN5  CAZN11  CAZN13  CA3ZN  CA5ZN3  
$ IM1  IM2  IM3  IM4  LAV_C14  LAV_C15  LAV_C36  
$ M21A3B2  MG2BA  MG2SI  MG17X2  MG23X6  
$ MG38SR9  MGZN  MG2ZN11  MG2ZN3  MG7ZN3  MN3SI  PHI  
$ SI_DIAMOND_A4  SRZN  SRZN5_LT  TAU

$**************************************************************************
$
$ A) Definition of elements
$ From A. T. Dinsdale, SGTE data for pure elements (Ref 0)
$
$**************************************************************************

$
$Element     Standard state   mass [g/mol]    enthalpy_298    entropy_298
ELEMENT VA   VACUUM           0.00             0.00              0.00     !
ELEMENT AL   FCC_A1           26.98154         4540.00           28.30    !
ELEMENT BA   BCC_A2           137.33           6910.00           62.50    ! 
ELEMENT CA   FCC_A1           40.078           5736.00           41.588   !
ELEMENT MG   HCP_A3           24.305           4998.00           32.671   !
ELEMENT MN   BCC_A12          54.938           4995.696          32.2206  !
ELEMENT SI   DIA_A4           28.0855          3217.00           18.81    !
ELEMENT SR   FCC_A1           87.62            6568.00           55.694   !
ELEMENT  Y   HCP_A3           88.9059          5966.384          44.4341  !
ELEMENT ZN   HCP_A3           65.38            5656.70           41.631   !
ELEMENT ZR   HCP_A3           91.224           5566.3            39.181   !

$**************************************************************************
$
$ B) MatCalc specific commands
$
$**************************************************************************
$
$ Defines MG as reference element
REFERENCE_ELEMENT MG !
$
$ if phase HCP_A3 is selected, add composition set for Zr particles ...
ADD_COMPOSITION_SET HCP_A3 :ZR:VA: !
$
$ if phase BCC_B2 is selected, add composition set for Zr particles ...
ADD_COMPOSITION_SET BCC_B2 :ZN:ZR: !
$
$ if phase YZZN2_A is selected, add composition set for Zr particles ...
ADD_COMPOSITION_SET YZZN2_A :ZR:: !
$
$ if phase YZZN2_B is selected, add composition set for Zr particles ...
ADD_COMPOSITION_SET YZZN2_B :ZR:: !
$
$ MatCalc syntax (MatCalc 5.23.1036) for split model of ordered phases
ATTACH_CONTRIBUTION MGY BCC_A2 ORDER_DISORDER !
$
$**************************************************************************
$ enthalpy of vacancy formation
$**************************************************************************
$
$ default for hcp_A3 is MG
PARAMETER HMVA(HCP_A3,*;0) 273.00 +86836.78; 6000.00  N
REF:pov11 !
$
PARAMETER HMVA(HCP_A3,AL:*;0) 273.00 +70000; 6000.00  N
REF:pov15 !
PARAMETER HMVA(HCP_A3,CA:*;0) 273.00 +70000; 6000.00  N
REF:pov15 !
PARAMETER HMVA(HCP_A3,MG:*;0) 273.00 +70000; 6000.00  N
REF:pov15 !
PARAMETER HMVA(HCP_A3,MN:*;0) 273.00 +70000; 6000.00  N
REF:pov15 !
PARAMETER HMVA(HCP_A3,SI:*;0) 273.00 +70000; 6000.00  N
REF:pov15 !
PARAMETER HMVA(HCP_A3,SR:*;0) 273.00 +70000; 6000.00  N
REF:pov15 !
PARAMETER HMVA(HCP_A3,ZN:*;0) 273.00 +70000; 6000.00  N
REF:pov15 !
